                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A setting of something to the account of; the attribution of personal guilt or personal righteousness of another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5a3252f-b546-4bb4-914a-8459442f8520",
                                                "sense_id": "a8d89809-bec2-3c50-ac37-783812a9271e",
                                                "text": "the imputation of the sin of Adam"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4636a002-8582-447d-81ce-a913465d8b51",
                                                "sense_id": "a8d89809-bec2-3c50-ac37-783812a9271e",
                                                "text": "the imputation of the righteousness of Christ"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a50d4cf4-8b82-495d-84b7-020d95f10659",
                                                "sense_id": "a8d89809-bec2-3c50-ac37-783812a9271e",
                                                "text": "So, if a Sonne that is by his Father ſent about Merchandize, doe ſinfully miſcarry vpon the Sea; the imputation of his vvickedneſſe, by your rule, ſhould be impoſed vpon his Father that ſent him: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0381e142-63d1-3de8-8a7a-f4b37010423c",
                                        "entry_id": "218a064e-7d2e-327d-b3ae-db940492818e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Opinion; intimation; hint."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0da4177-a2dc-4292-83de-5133215c9c81",
                                                "sense_id": "0381e142-63d1-3de8-8a7a-f4b37010423c",
                                                "text": "All the legends of the past, and all the stupefying imputations of Henry Akeley’s letters and exhibits, welled up in my memory to heighten the atmosphere of tension and growing menace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
